# Next.js Coding Rules (App Router) — Kovia WMS FE

## Read the relevant source of truth

This file holds the mandatory core rules. For the area being changed, read the linked document; do not copy its detailed rules into another document.

| Work                                                                     | Required document                                                                |
| ------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Folder layout, ownership, data flow, hooks, forms, refactor triggers     | [FOLDER_STRUCTURE.md](docs/FOLDER_STRUCTURE.md)                                  |
| Reuse, shadcn/ui primitives, helpers, abstractions, clean code checklist | [CODING_GUIDELINES.md](docs/CODING_GUIDELINES.md)                                |
| Visual system (Kovia UI)                                                 | [DESIGN_SYSTEM.md](docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md)                                        |
| List/table screens                                                       | [LIST_TABLE_DESIGN_GUIDELINES.md](docs/LIST_TABLE_DESIGN_GUIDELINES.md)          |
| Design tokens                                                            | `src/app/index.css`                                                              |
| Branches, commits, PRs                                                   | [GIT_WORKFLOW.md](docs/GIT_WORKFLOW.md)                                          |

Authority: this file and FOLDER_STRUCTURE.md define code architecture and ownership. DESIGN_SYSTEM.md and LIST_TABLE_DESIGN_GUIDELINES.md own UI. A description of existing code is not an exemption from these rules.

## General
- Correctness and clarity over speed. Accessibility and preservation of user data are required.
- Comments only explain *why*, never *what*.
- Reuse existing code/patterns. Add to an existing file when the change belongs to that file's responsibility; otherwise extract a focused module.
- Prefer the smallest complete change. No speculative layers, generic controllers, wrappers, or dependencies.
- No generic names like `index.tsx` at the feature root — use explicit names like `WarehouseOverview.tsx`. Exception: `index.tsx` is allowed as the entry point of a named subfolder (the folder name IS the component name, e.g. `TaskAssignmentScoring/index.tsx`). Next.js special filenames (`page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, …) are also exceptions.
- No abbreviated variable names (`error` not `err`, `button` not `btn`).
- Before changing a boundary, identify callers, props/types, exports, schemas, services, query keys, and affected tests.
- Keep existing validation, permission checks, error handling, and cleanup when moving code.

## File Naming
| Type | Convention |
|------|-----------|
| Feature folder | `kebab-case` (`stock-issue`, `inbound-request`) |
| Component | `PascalCase.tsx` |
| Feature page | `<Name>Page.tsx` in `pages/` |
| Hook | `use-kebab-case.ts` |
| Service | `kebab-case.service.ts` |
| Store | `kebab-case.store.ts` |
| Schema | `kebab-case.schema.ts` |
| Types | `kebab-case.types.ts` |
| Pure helper / mapper | `kebab-case.ts` in `utils/`, named by behavior (`stock-issue-format.ts`, `layout-scene-mapper.ts`) |
| Next.js entry | As Next.js requires: `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`, … |

## Exports
- **Feature pages only**: Default Export. Route `page.tsx` imports it directly or through the feature's `pages/index.ts` (`export { default as InventoryPage } from './InventoryPage'`).
- **Next.js special files**: the export shape Next.js requires.
- **Everything else**: Named Export.
- **Component subdirectories** (`components/<PageName>/`): must have an `index.ts` barrel that re-exports all named exports. Pages import from the barrel (`../components/WarehouseDetailPage`), not individual files.
- Inside a feature prefer relative imports; use `@/` for `src/components`, `src/lib`, `src/config`, `src/routes`, `src/hooks`, `src/stores`, `src/types` and other features.

## Folder Structure
```
src/features/<feature>/
├── pages/           # Default exports, rendered by app/**/page.tsx (thin shells — compose + coordinate)
├── components/      # Feature UI components
│   └── <PageName>/  # Sub-components for a specific page (dialogs, sheets, tables) + index.ts barrel
│       └── <ViewName>/  # Nested subfolder when a sub-view has its own clear responsibility (review signal: ~150 lines)
│           ├── index.tsx    # Entry point — named export of the view
│           ├── types.ts     # Local types shared within this view only
│           └── *.tsx        # Sub-components
├── hooks/           # React Query hooks, form/behavior/workflow hooks
├── services/        # Axios wrappers (plain objects)
├── schemas/         # Zod schemas + inferred types
├── types/           # Feature DTO / view-model types
└── utils/           # Pure feature-only helpers and mappers
```
Route entries → `src/app/(private)/**/page.tsx`, `src/app/(public)/**/page.tsx`
Shared primitives → `src/components/ui/`; shared app components → `src/components/{layout,operations,forms,barcode}/`
Zustand stores → `src/stores/`
Full map and ownership table: [docs/FOLDER_STRUCTURE.md](docs/FOLDER_STRUCTURE.md). Create only the folders a feature actually uses.

## No God-Class Pages
- Route `page.tsx` stays thin: await/forward route params or `searchParams`, redirects, metadata, and render the feature page. No business logic, hooks, or API calls.
- Pages must NOT contain component definitions. Each dialog, sheet, or complex sub-component gets its own file.
- Place page sub-components in `components/<PageName>/` (e.g., `WarehouseDetailPage/WarehouseEditDialog.tsx`).
- Pages are thin shells: fetch API data via hooks, pass data down as props, compose layout. No business logic in pages.
- Orchestrator components (e.g., `TaskAssignmentScoring`) own UI state (dialogs, filters) and pass callbacks to children.
- A hook owns one cohesive behavior/resource/workflow. Moving a whole page into one hook or one orchestrator does not solve a God Component.
- Pages import from the barrel (`components/<PageName>`), not individual files.
- Internal imports within the same `<PageName>/` folder stay relative (sibling-to-sibling).
- Internal imports within a `<ViewName>/` subfolder also stay relative. Siblings import each other directly (`./StockIssueRequestLines`), not through the barrel.
- Types shared only within a `<ViewName>/` folder go in `types.ts` inside that folder, not in `features/<feature>/types/`.

## Data Flow (bắt buộc)

```
app/**/page.tsx → features/<feature>/pages/<Name>Page
  Page → owns API hooks (useQuery / useMutation) + server state
    └── Component → display only, receives data and callbacks via props
Page / orchestrator → feature hook → service → axiosClient → BE
```

- **Pages** call all React Query hooks. Pass `data`, `isLoading`, `isPending`, and callback functions (`onSubmit`, `onDelete`, `onEdit`) as props to components.
- **Components** (dialogs, sheets, tables) must NOT import or call any React Query hooks or services. They are pure UI — receive props, render, call callbacks. Local UI state (open, focus, hover) is fine.
- **Exception**: Orchestrator components that own a distinct sub-domain (e.g., `TaskAssignmentScoring` managing its own dialogs and filters) may call hooks for that sub-domain only, as long as the parent page does not also manage the same data.
- Pages and orchestrators also reach HTTP only through hooks — never call `*Service.*` directly. Pure helpers/mappers from `utils/` may be called directly.

## Validation (Zod schemas)

- All Zod schemas live in `features/<feature>/schemas/<name>.schema.ts`.
- Schema file exports: the `z.object(...)` schema and the inferred TypeScript type (`type Foo = z.infer<typeof fooSchema>`).
- Pages or orchestrators import the schema to wire `useForm({ resolver: zodResolver(schema) })`, directly or through a focused form hook they call once.
- Components receive `form` (from `useForm`) as a prop — they do NOT call `useForm` themselves. One logical form = one owner = one `useForm` instance; never a second instance for the same form.
- Separate schemas per BE Command (Create vs Update use different schema files when the commands differ).

## Error Handling
- Never swallow errors silently.
- Always: `logger.error(error)` (from `@/lib/logger`) + `toast.error('...')` via Sonner. Never use `console.error` or `console.log` directly — use `logger.*` instead. `logger` strips stack traces in prod automatically.
- All async operations handle 3 states: `loading`, `error`, `success`.
- Use early returns for loading/error to keep render clean.
- Load failures render `ErrorState` (`@/components/ErrorState`) or `OperationalState` with the original `unknown` error; do not treat any HTTP error as "no data".
- Each failed user action has one reporting owner (the mutation or workflow hook); do not report the same error again in the caller.
- Never show success after a failed step. Keep dirty input, block duplicate submission for the whole workflow, and surface partial success with a safe retry path.

## State
- Never mutate state directly — use immutable setter patterns.
- Minimize `useEffect`. Derive state during render when possible.
- `useEffect` with subscriptions/timers must return a cleanup function.
- Keep effect dependencies correct; do not disable `react-hooks/exhaustive-deps` to force a lifecycle.
- Hooks run at the top level. Lazy data uses `enabled` or a conditionally mounted orchestrator, never conditional hook calls.
- Do not mirror query data into local state or a store. An editable form draft is intentional local state.

## State Management
- **Client/UI state** (auth, preferences, UI flags) → Zustand in `src/stores/`.
- **Server state** (API data) → React Query. Never store server data in Zustand.
- Local state stays local; state lives in the lowest owner that needs to coordinate it.
- React Query hooks live in `features/<feature>/hooks/`.
- Query keys must be arrays containing every relevant parameter: `['resource', params]`. Reuse `queryKeys` from `src/lib/query-keys.ts`; do not define the same query in two places.
- Always handle `onError` in mutations.
- Load only visible/needed data, filter at BE, and paginate with `OperationalPagination`; never "fetch everything" to count or filter on the client.

## Service Layer
- Services are plain objects, not classes.
- Import the Axios instance `axiosClient` from `src/lib/axios.ts`. Do not create another Axios instance or attach tokens in feature code.
- Endpoint paths come from `API_ENDPOINTS` in `src/routes/api-endpoints.ts`; never hardcode hosts or paths in features.
- Return business data by unwrapping the actual envelope (`response.data.data` for `ApiResponse<T>`, `response.data` for Blob); never return the full Axios response.
- Do not catch errors in services — let React Query handle them.
- Services do not own React state, toast, dialogs, or navigation.

## Forms
- Use React Hook Form + Zod. Define Zod schema first, infer TS type from it.
- No manual validation logic when Zod can express it. Cross-field rules live in the schema or a pure function.
- Field errors from `form.formState.errors`, not global state. Map BE validation errors to the matching field.
- Distinguish create/edit/duplicate; reset or remount deliberately when the entity changes; a background refetch must not overwrite dirty fields.

## Styling
- Tailwind CSS **v4** (CSS-first config in `src/app/index.css` via `@theme`; no `tailwind.config.js` — uses `@tailwindcss/postcss`).
- When copying components from shadcn/ui, use the Tailwind v4 versions (current default). v4 syntax like `w-(--var)` is valid here.
- Tailwind CSS only. Class order: layout → spacing → typography → colors → states.
- Conditional/merged classes always use `cn()` from `src/lib/utils.ts`.
- Component variants use CVA (`class-variance-authority`).
- Do not manually reorder Tailwind classes — `prettier-plugin-tailwindcss` handles it.

## Animation (bắt buộc)

Animation library: `tw-animate-css` (imported in `src/app/index.css`). Use `data-[state=open]:` / `data-[state=closed]:` syntax — NOT `data-open:` / `data-closed:` — to match Radix UI's `data-state` attribute.

### Mọi overlay / modal / dialog

```
data-[state=open]:animate-in data-[state=open]:fade-in-0 data-[state=open]:zoom-in-95 data-[state=open]:slide-in-from-bottom-4
data-[state=closed]:animate-out data-[state=closed]:fade-out-0 data-[state=closed]:zoom-out-95 data-[state=closed]:slide-out-to-bottom-2
animation-duration-250
```

### Mọi dropdown / popover / select content

```
data-[state=open]:animate-in data-[state=open]:fade-in-0 data-[state=open]:zoom-in-95
data-[state=closed]:animate-out data-[state=closed]:fade-out-0 data-[state=closed]:zoom-out-95
data-[side=bottom]:slide-in-from-top-2 data-[side=top]:slide-in-from-bottom-2
data-[side=left]:slide-in-from-right-2 data-[side=right]:slide-in-from-left-2
animation-duration-200
```

### Sheet / Drawer

```
data-[state=open]:animate-in data-[state=open]:slide-in-from-right
data-[state=closed]:animate-out data-[state=closed]:slide-out-to-right
animation-duration-300
```

### Duration chuẩn

| Loại | Duration |
|------|----------|
| Dropdown / Select / Tooltip | 200ms |
| Dialog / Modal | 250ms |
| Sheet / Drawer | 300ms |
| Micro-interaction (button, badge) | 150ms |

- Dùng `animation-duration-*` (tw-animate-css utility, set `--tw-animation-duration`) — KHÔNG dùng `duration-*` (Tailwind transition utility, không ảnh hưởng animation).
- Easing mặc định: `ease` (enter). Sheet dùng `ease-out`.

## Dropdown Alignment (bắt buộc)

- **`SelectContent` luôn dùng `align="start"`** (không để mặc định `center` — gây lệch sang giữa).
- **`DropdownMenuContent`** dùng `align="end"` khi mở từ góc phải (avatar, action menu), `align="start"` cho menu bên trái.
- **`PopoverContent`** dùng `align="start"` mặc định trừ khi thiết kế yêu cầu khác.
- Không dùng `position="item-aligned"` trong Select (gây scroll container clipping trong Dialog).
- Luôn thêm `sideOffset={4}` để dropdown không dính vào trigger.

## Fixed Viewport Layout (bắt buộc cho trang có bảng)

`docs/LIST_TABLE_DESIGN_GUIDELINES.md` và `OperationalListPanel` là source of truth cho bố cục list/table. Mọi màn hình mới hoặc được refactor phải dùng pattern này; không sao chép công thức chiều cao viewport vào feature.

Mọi page có bảng dữ liệu phải dùng cấu trúc sau — không để browser scroll toàn trang:

```tsx
// Page root
<div className="h-full flex flex-col bg-background text-foreground">
  {/* page header — shrink-0 */}

  <div className="flex min-h-0 min-w-0 w-full flex-1 flex-col gap-4 px-4 py-5 md:px-8">
    <div className="… shrink-0">             {/* title + actions */}
    <div className="… shrink-0">             {/* search / filters */}

    {/* Table card — luôn chiếm toàn bộ chiều cao còn lại */}
    <OperationalListPanel>
      <Table>
        <TableHeader className="sticky top-0 z-10 bg-card">…</TableHeader>
        <TableBody>…</TableBody>
      </Table>
    </OperationalListPanel>
  </div>
</div>
```

- Root: `h-full flex flex-col` (không dùng `min-h-full`)
- Content wrapper: `w-full min-w-0 flex-1 min-h-0` — bắt buộc; không dùng `mx-auto`, `container` hoặc `max-w-*` cho workspace/list nghiệp vụ
- Toolbar/header: `shrink-0` — không bị co lại
- Scroll chỉ xảy ra bên trong table card, không phải toàn trang
- `OperationalListPanel` quản lý `flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-hidden`; không chép các class này vào feature.
- Direct child `[data-slot=table-container]` hoặc `[data-slot=operational-list-body]` là vùng `overflow-auto` duy nhất.
- `TableHead` dùng `sticky top-0 z-10 bg-card` để header đứng yên khi body cuộn.

### Bảng có pagination (Pattern C)

Đặt `Table` và `OperationalPagination` làm con trực tiếp của `OperationalListPanel`:

```tsx
<OperationalListPanel>
  <Table>…</Table>
  <OperationalPagination … />
</OperationalListPanel>
```

- Không dùng `calc(100vh - ...)`; flex layout tự tính chiều cao còn lại và ổn định khi zoom
- Sticky dùng per-cell (`<TableHead className="sticky top-0 z-10 bg-card">`).
- Pagination state (`page`, `pageSize`) luôn nằm ở Page, truyền xuống component qua props

## TypeScript
- No `any`. Use `unknown` and narrow the type, or define a proper type.
- No type assertions (`as SomeType`) unless unavoidable — add a comment explaining why.
- Prefer `interface` for object shapes, `type` for unions/intersections/aliases.
- Derive types from source of truth — never duplicate: use `z.infer<>` from Zod schemas, `ReturnType<>`, `Parameters<>`, `Awaited<>` when applicable.
- Use `type` keyword for type-only imports: `import type { StockIssueRequest } from '../types/stock-issue.types'`.
- Mark optional props explicitly with `?`. Never use `| undefined` manually when `?` suffices.
- Use `readonly` for props/state that should not be mutated.
- Avoid enums — use `as const` objects or Zod `z.enum()` instead.

## Component Props
- Explicit TypeScript interfaces for all props. No `any`.
- Destructure props in function signature.
- Type-only imports use `import type { ... }`.

## Routing, runtime and hydration
- App Router only: `next/navigation` (`useRouter`, `redirect`), `next/link`. Route loading uses `loading.tsx` / `<Suspense>`.
- URLs come from `APP_ROUTES` in `src/routes/app-routes.ts`; never hardcode feature URLs.
- Pure navigation uses `Link` (or `Button asChild`) with `href`. Imperative navigation (`useRouter`) is only for action completion, confirmed discard, auth redirects, or URL-state sync — inside components or hooks, never in services.
- Protected routes: reuse `src/proxy.ts`, `ProtectedRoute` (checks `useAuthStore`) in `app/(private)/layout.tsx`, and `src/config/route-permissions.ts`. Do not add a parallel guard. FE gating never replaces BE authorization.
- Default to Server Components. Place `'use client'` at the smallest necessary interactive boundary (normally the feature page); never import server-only code into its subtree. Props crossing into client components must be serializable.
- Keep server and first client render identical: no `window`/`document`/storage reads, current dates, or random values during shared render. Read browser values in effects/events; use `useId` for IDs.
- `suppressHydrationWarning` only on the single intentionally differing element, never to hide a subtree mismatch.
- Client env variables use `NEXT_PUBLIC_`; secrets stay server-only and out of git.

## Role and permission codes
- Declare frontend permission codes only in `src/config/permissionCodes.ts`; route access in `src/config/route-permissions.ts`. Components render from capability props (`canCreate`, `canUpdate`, …) supplied by their page. Full rules: `AGENTS.md` → "Role and permission changes".

## BE–FE Contract (bắt buộc)

Before writing any form/service/schema for a feature, read the corresponding BE Command, Validator and Response files. Then:

1. **Field names must match exactly** — use the same casing as the BE DTO (camelCase in JSON). No aliases, no renaming.
2. **Zod schema must mirror BE validator** — every `NotEmpty`, `MaximumLength`, `MinimumLength`, `GreaterThan`, `EmailAddress`, etc. must have an equivalent Zod rule. Check handler/domain rules too, not only the validator file.
3. **Service payload must match the BE Command** — only send fields the BE Command declares. Never send extra or UI-only fields; never omit required ones.
4. **Separate Create vs Update schemas** when BE Commands differ (e.g. `createWarehouseSchema` has `warehouseCode` + `warehouseName`, `updateWarehouseSchema` has no `warehouseCode`). Use `z.object` per command, not one shared schema.
5. **Response types must include all fields the BE returns** — read the BE `*Response.cs` before writing the TS interface.
6. **When BE adds/removes a field, update in this order**: schema → types → service → hook → component.
7. **PUT that replaces a child list** (e.g. document lines): send every row that remains; do not send line IDs the command does not accept.

## Architecture quality gate
- One responsibility per page/orchestrator/hook; one owner per state/form; no hidden whole-screen controller.
- Review signals: page/orchestrator >~250 nonblank lines, hook/view >~150, >~10 top-level inputs/outputs, props passed through 3+ layers, several effects syncing the same data. They trigger review, not mechanical splitting; explain a cohesive exception.
- Complete the detailed gate in [FOLDER_STRUCTURE.md](docs/FOLDER_STRUCTURE.md) §9 and the checklist in [CODING_GUIDELINES.md](docs/CODING_GUIDELINES.md).
- Run `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint` and relevant `pnpm test` (Vitest, setup `src/config/test-setup.ts`). Non-trivial new logic or workflows need a focused check. Report checks not run. Documentation-only changes need link, consistency and scope checks, not a full build.
